{"content": "Hange then begins explaining about the two Titans they have captured and the tests being done to them, including attempts to communicate. The Titans were named Sawney and Beane, after a human tribe that used to eat humans. The experiment continued as they tried to deprive the Titans of sunlight. Afterward, they tested whether the Titans have any other vulnerabilities by directly damaging their bodies, which caused pain for Hange as well. Hearing Hange talking about the Titans like that, Eren questions how is it that Hange is able to stay so cheerful around the Titans. Hange explains that they used to hate them as well, but after a certain incident, they realized the mystery of Titans' bodies and tried to look at them from a different point of view since then. Seeing that not only Hange, but the whole Scout Regiment are people who desire change, Eren asks Hange to tell him more about their experiments, however, even after a whole night, he seemingly learns nothing new.", "chunk_index": 3, "source_url": "https://attackontitan.fandom.com/wiki/Special_Operations_Squad:_Eve_of_the_Counterattack,_Part_2", "source_title": "Special Operations Squad: Eve of the Counterattack, Part 2", "source_type": "episode", "episode_number": 15, "entity": null, "reveal_episode": 15, "embedding": [-0.06328321993350983, 0.02955789491534233, 0.05562131106853485, 0.07765985280275345, 0.057076338678598404, -0.07119641453027725, 0.11063630133867264, 0.017291836440563202, -0.07678163051605225, -0.019563714042305946, -0.07184475660324097, -0.02978367917239666, -0.007621881552040577, -0.039547163993120193, 0.03029165044426918, -0.029349198564887047, -0.0068685198202729225, -0.00485675735399127, -0.027792977169156075, -0.012754913419485092, -0.021816719323396683, 0.038386959582567215, 0.06270758807659149, 0.10037330538034439, -0.06401687860488892, -0.08424180001020432, 0.019637053832411766, -0.0689716786146164, 0.002987803192809224, -0.04891194775700569, 0.02126043103635311, -0.0284463